Sval: list only the OS's own speech voices for the UI language

A new RFPTarget, SpeechVoicesDefault, limits speechSynthesis.getVoices to
the OS's default voice and the voices for the UI language the user did not
download, so neither installed voices nor the OS's full voice set reaches a
page while speech keeps working. It is Doc-gated, so granularOverrides gives
a site the full list.

Gecko's backends cannot all tell a shipped voice from a downloaded one.
macOS can, by identifier: voices downloaded in Settings are
com.apple.voice.enhanced.* and com.apple.voice.premium.*, and
SvalRFPService::IsDefaultSpeechVoice hides them. SapiService (Windows) and
SpeechDispatcherService (Linux) register only a name, language and URI with
no such mark, so there the list is limited by language alone. The macOS
identifier scheme is Apple's, read from AVSpeechSynthesisVoice identifiers;
it was not checked against a downloaded voice.

No chrome API can change what SpeechSynthesis::GetVoices lists.

